.TH SDL_LockTextureToSurface 3 "SDL 3.5.0" "Simple Directmedia Layer" "SDL3 FUNCTIONS"
.SH NAME
SDL_LockTextureToSurface \- Lock a portion of the texture for
.BR write-only
pixel access, and expose it as a SDL surface.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <SDL3/SDL_render.h>
.PP
.BI "bool SDL_LockTextureToSurface(SDL_Texture *texture, const SDL_Rect *rect, SDL_Surface **surface);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Besides providing an
.BR SDL_Surface
instead of raw pixel data, this function operates like
.BR SDL_LockTexture \[char46]
.PP
As an optimization, the pixels made available for editing don\(aqt necessarily contain the old texture data\[char46] This is a write-only operation, and if you need to keep a copy of the texture data you should do that at the application level\[char46]
.PP
You must use
.BR SDL_UnlockTexture ()
to unlock the pixels and apply any changes\[char46]
.PP
The returned surface is freed internally after calling
.BR SDL_UnlockTexture ()
or
.BR SDL_DestroyTexture ()\[char46]
The caller should not free it\[char46]

.SH FUNCTION PARAMETERS
.TP
.I texture
the texture to lock for access, which must be created with
.BR SDL_TEXTUREACCESS_STREAMING \[char46]

.TP
.I rect
a pointer to the rectangle to lock for access\[char46] If the rect is NULL, the entire texture will be locked\[char46]
.TP
.I surface
a pointer to an SDL surface of size
.BR rect \[char46]
Don\(aqt assume any specific pixel content\[char46]
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns true on success or false on failure; call
.BR SDL_GetError ()
for more information\[char46]

.SH THREAD SAFETY
This function should only be called on the main thread\[char46]

.SH AVAILABILITY
This function is available since SDL 3\[char46]2\[char46]0\[char46]

.SH SEE ALSO
.BR SDL_LockTexture (3),
.BR SDL_UnlockTexture (3)
